35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The data is stark: February hit 29,400 yen, August dropped to 9,100. No two months are close. A fixed rate would just hide this volatility, not solve it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, that volatility is scary, but my findings show the real cost is time. The template meant keying in every invoice, and the other house spent forty minutes just logging readings.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The monitor showed one room drawing four times another. The sunlight data confirms two rooms need heat much earlier. The old equal split is definitely unfair.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The volatility is extreme, and the metering quote is steep. I need to see how these numbers actually translate into our monthly reality before I can agree to anything.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found the cooler notice stayed up all summer. People sweated rather than argue. The payment log shows late payments after queries. The money really did make us distant.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, forty minutes is manageable, but the template’s manual entry is a nightmare. @Jonathan, that four-to-one gap proves the flat split is broken. We need a system that reflects actual usage, not just averages.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, forty minutes is fine, but the template meant keying in every single invoice by hand. That’s a whole evening gone, not just a quick check.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I hear you. But if the system is fair, the arguing stops. I’d rather spend an evening once than resent the split for a year.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, I hear the fairness argument, but the upfront cost for metering is 170,000 yen. I cannot commit to that expense without knowing if the savings justify it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, I’m sorry the cost worries you. But seeing the late payments, I think we need to fix the trust first, not just the money.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the upfront cost is high, but consider the alternative: resentment. If we don’t fix the usage gap, the bills will keep eating our relationships.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, resentment is real, but so is the time. If the ""fair"" system eats my whole evening, I’m not doing it. We need something that doesn’t demand a full-time job.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I understand the time concern. But the monitor data shows the gap is real. A fair system might actually save us time by ending the arguments.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, resentment is expensive, but so is a 170,000 yen investment. I need to know if the savings actually cover that upfront cost before I can agree to metering.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Mio, I agree. If it takes too long, I won’t do it. I just want us to be kind, not tired.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
